.TH "RAPTOR-LIBRARY" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-library \- part types and assemblies: list, apply, insert, sync
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor library\fR [\-h] ACTION ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
A part type is an element's data without identity or placement; an assembly is a saved group of elements (a hierarchy with its contents, a node with its blocks, events) with its internal links. A library is a plain JSON file of both. Applying a part type writes ordinary columns and records a link; inserting an assembly adds a fresh copy with new ids and free names, so the model stays a normal model. The model file changes only for apply/save/detach/insert.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBlist\fR
list the parts in a library
.TP
\fBshow\fR
show one part type
.TP
\fBimport\fR
import a legacy .rbl/.json library
.TP
\fBadd\fR
save a model block as a new part type
.TP
\fBinsert\fR
insert a copy of an assembly into a model
.TP
\fBapply\fR
apply a part type to blocks and link them
.TP
\fBsync\fR
show or apply changed part types
.TP
\fBdetach\fR
drop a block's link, keeping its values
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY LIST
\fBraptor library list\fR [\-h] [\-f {text,json}] FILE
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY SHOW
\fBraptor library show\fR [\-h] [\-f {text,json}] FILE PART
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY IMPORT
\fBraptor library import\fR [\-h] [\-\-name N] [\-\-force] FILE SOURCE
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIN\fR
name of the new library
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
replace an existing library file
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY ADD
\fBraptor library add\fR [\-h] (\-\-block NAME|ID | \-\-assembly NAMES) [\-\-kind {block,node,event,hierarchy,annotation}] [\-\-name N] [\-\-category TEXT] [\-\-source TEXT] [\-\-basis {data,handbook,experience}] FILE MODEL
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-block\fR \fINAME|ID\fR
the element whose values become a part type
.TP
\fB\-\-assembly\fR \fINAMES\fR
comma list of elements saved as an assembly (a hierarchy brings everything inside it)
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI{block|node|event|hierarchy|annotation}\fR
what \-\-block names (default block)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIN\fR
part name (default: the element's)
.TP
\fB\-\-category\fR \fITEXT\fR
group the part is listed under
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fITEXT\fR
where the numbers came from: a handbook, a test report, a person
.TP
\fB\-\-basis\fR \fI{data|handbook|experience}\fR
where the numbers came from (judgement is read as experience)
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY INSERT
\fBraptor library insert\fR [\-h] \-\-library FILE \-\-part PART [\-\-at X,Y] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}] MODEL
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fIFILE\fR
the .rbdlib to read
.TP
\fB\-\-part\fR \fIPART\fR
assembly name or id
.TP
\fB\-\-at\fR \fIX,Y\fR
model position of the copy's top\-left (default: right of the model)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the change back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY APPLY
\fBraptor library apply\fR [\-h] \-\-library FILE \-\-part PART \-\-blocks NAMES [\-\-override FIELDS] [\-\-in\-place] MODEL
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fIFILE\fR
the .rbdlib to read
.TP
\fB\-\-part\fR \fIPART\fR
part type name or id
.TP
\fB\-\-blocks\fR \fINAMES\fR
comma list of block names or ids
.TP
\fB\-\-override\fR \fIFIELDS\fR
comma list of fields to leave as they are
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the changes back to MODEL
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY SYNC
\fBraptor library sync\fR [\-h] \-\-library FILE [\-\-apply] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}] MODEL
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fIFILE\fR
the .rbdlib to compare with
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
write the pending changes (default: report only)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
with \-\-apply, write back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR LIBRARY DETACH
\fBraptor library detach\fR [\-h] \-\-block NAME|ID [\-\-in\-place] MODEL
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-block\fR \fINAME|ID\fR
the linked block
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the change back to MODEL
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Save a hierarchy, with everything inside it, as an assembly.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor library add parts.rbdlib plant.rbds \-\-assembly "Gen bank" \-\-name "Generator bank"\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Insert a fresh copy of it into a model and save the model.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor library insert plant.rbds \-\-library parts.rbdlib \-\-part "Generator bank" \-\-at 40,10 \-\-in\-place\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
